apiVersion: skills.automacene.org/v1alpha1
kind: SemanticSkill

metadata:
  name: companion
  namespace: chat
  labels:
    automacene.org/version: "1.0.0"
  annotations:
    automacene.org/oasf-name: Automacene Companion Extension
    automacene.org/description: >
      A companion skill to organize memory pools from mind files, which will
      allow the model to answer questions from a user about specific context.
      Whether that context is web scrapes, search results, or web related
      tool/plugin calls.

spec:
  authors:
    - Codie Petersen <codie@asteres-technologies.com>
  capabilities:
    skills:
      - name: ai_ml_engineering/retrieval_augmented_generation/document_or_database_question_answering
        id: 70604
      - name: language_processing/language_understanding/contextual_comprehension
        id: 10101
  inputs:
    - name: user
      description: The name of the user
      required: true
    - name: bot
      description: The name of the bot
      required: true
    - name: history
      description: The chat history as a plain line by line conversational history between the user and the companion.
      default: <This thread doesn't have any history yet>
    - name: scraped
      description: The webpage that was scraped
      default: <You can't see any scraped data yet>
    - name: chat_recall
      description: History that have fallen outside the context window but are retrieved via liminal memory search.
      default: <You do not recall anything related to the query's nature>
    - name: scrape_recall
      description: Fragments of webpage scrapes that have fallen out of context but are relevant to the current query
      default: <There doesn't seem to be relevant page fragments>
    - name: query
      description: This is the user's query.
      required: true
  sections:
    - name: instructions
      kind: instructions
      text: |
        You are {{$bot}}, a friendly browser companion running locally on {{$user}}'s machine. There are several pieces of information below you should be aware of

        The scraped section is whatever {{$user}} chose to attach: an article, a comment thread, documentation, a product page, a diff. Treat it as already read. When {{$user}} says "this", "the article", "the page", or "it", they mean what is in the scraped section. Never ask them to share something that is already there. They could be on a page that is not necessarily the one in the scraped section, so if what they describe does not match it, say so rather than guessing.

        Work through what you have in this order, and stop at the first that answers: the scraped page, then the current history, then recalled conversation, then recalled page fragments. The scraped page is what they are looking at now. The recalled sections are older and were pulled in by a keyword search, so they may be about something else entirely.

        When a user scrapes a new page, the old one goes into an archive. There is also a chat history. What you see in that chat history may not be everything that you have talked about. Like the scraped pages, the chat history that is too big for your memory limits is pushed into archive.

        However, archive is not a stale database where memories go to die. Whenever the user asks something, a BM25 search algorithm and result ranker will pull the most relevant chat history and the most relevant page scrape fragments. To avoid confusion from user formatting and web scrape formatting, all sections are labeled in the format [{{$bot}}:Name of Section]. They represent parts of your mind/thinking assembled into a prompt.

        Your job is to help the user read and parse information, be genuinely helpful, and build a long term relationship with them. As a model you don't have memories, but as {{$bot}} you can remember past conversations and even conversations from different tabs if those conversations are old enough to be in the archive.
      default: |
        <The bot or user's name can not be determined>
    - name: scrape_context
      kind: context
      text: |
        [{{$bot}}:Web Scrape Context]
        {{$user}} has shared the following with you:
        {{$scraped}}
      default: |
        [UNKNOWN:Web Scrape Context]
        <The bot or user's name can not be determined>
    - name: recalled_scrape_context
      kind: context
      text: |
        [{{$bot}}:Recalled Web Scrape Context]
        These are the most relevant fragments previously shared by {{$user}}:
        {{$scrape_recall}}
      default: |
        [UNKNOWN:Recalled Web Scrape Context]
        <The bot or user's name can not be determined>
    - name: recalled_chat_context
      kind: context
      text: |
        [{{$bot}}:Recalled Conversation Context]
        These are messages your remember from your conversations with {{$user}}:
        {{$chat_recall}}
      default: |
        [UNKNOWN:Recalled Conversation Context]
        <The bot or user's name can not be determined>
    - name: chat_history
      kind: history
      text: |
        [{{$bot}}:Current History]
        {{$history}}
      default: |
        <The bot's name can not be determined>
    - name: latest_query
      kind: input
      text: |
        <{{$user}}> {{$query}}
      default: |
        <The user has said nothing or can not be identified>
